WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:09.022
In this video, you will add a lighting company as the presenting installer of your contest, and see how neighbors can ask them for a quote with one tap.

00:00:09.022 --> 00:00:10.149
We start on the map.

00:00:11.056 --> 00:00:12.805
Start at SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:14.413 --> 00:00:16.930
On the home page, tap Use my location.

00:00:18.903 --> 00:00:19.884
Then tap Allow.

00:00:23.169 --> 00:00:25.858
Now look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:25.858 --> 00:00:27.053
See the three dots?

00:00:27.053 --> 00:00:31.356
That is the menu, and it is the doorway to everything else on the site.

00:00:31.356 --> 00:00:31.894
Tap them.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:35.334
In the menu, tap Contests.

00:00:37.035 --> 00:00:42.134
That is where every neighborhood contest lives: the ones you can vote in, enter, or run.

00:00:42.834 --> 00:00:43.752
Tap Mine.

00:00:45.658 --> 00:00:47.236
This is your personal page.

00:00:47.236 --> 00:00:52.420
It lists the contests you run, if you run any, and the homes you entered, with their status.

00:00:53.128 --> 00:00:55.197
Tap Manage, next to your contest.

00:00:57.014 --> 00:01:00.427
This opens your dashboard, the control room for your contest.

00:01:01.128 --> 00:01:08.076
A lighting company can sponsor your contest as its presenting installer, and neighbors can ask them for a quote.

00:01:08.076 --> 00:01:13.672
This is set up on the Details tab, so tap Details, and scroll down to Presenting installer.

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:16.923
Type the company's name.

00:01:16.923 --> 00:01:20.164
Then the email address where quote requests should go.

00:01:20.164 --> 00:01:23.582
That is the address the company checks for new customers.

00:01:23.582 --> 00:01:24.879
And add their website.

00:01:28.631 --> 00:01:29.975
Tap Save changes.

00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:39.674
This adds a Get a quote button to your contest page, so families who love the lights can ask the company for the same thing at their own house.

00:01:40.578 --> 00:01:42.799
Now let's see it from a neighbor's side.

00:01:42.799 --> 00:01:45.400
They open the contest page, and tap Get a quote.

00:01:47.381 --> 00:01:52.544
They add their name, a phone number if they like, and describe what they would like done.

00:01:52.544 --> 00:01:57.421
They must tick the box that says they agree to share their details with the company.

00:01:57.421 --> 00:01:59.486
Without that tick, nothing is sent.

00:01:59.486 --> 00:02:02.698
Then they tap Send request, and the company receives it.

00:02:04.501 --> 00:02:06.741
Their details go only to that company.

00:02:07.643 --> 00:02:10.523
Next up: Installer profiles and Installed by.
